    "custom_collections_describe_gMRkak": {
      "type": "custom-collections-describe",
      "blocks": {
        "describe_card_mjJeaD": {
          "type": "describe_card",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Precision Power for Perfect Lift",
            "content": "Throttle response matters most when pulling a clean wheelie. The Macfox X7 and X1S deliver smooth rear-drive torque that lifts predictably without jerks, while the X2’s dual-suspension setup absorbs landings and gives confidence on mixed terrain. Every model uses a 48 V power system tuned for instant acceleration and controlled balance — not brute force."
          }
        },
        "describe_card_FX7BVr": {
          "type": "describe_card",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Geometry That Keeps You Centered",
            "content": "True wheelie control comes from smart frame design. Macfox bikes use optimized seat height, longer swingarms, and centered battery placement to help you find and hold the balance point. This means fewer accidental flips and more time fine-tuning your throttle rhythm."
          }
        },
        "describe_card_qW3Y6Q": {
          "type": "describe_card",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Style That Speaks for Itself",
            "content": "From the minimalist X1S × Bs.Zay edition to the bold stance of the X7, every Macfox wheelie e-bike turns heads. Custom colorways, fat-tire confidence, and clean street lines make each trick look effortless. Whether you ride for fun or for footage, these bikes amplify your personality."
          }
        },
        "describe_card_PA7xnE": {
          "type": "describe_card",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A Community Built on Motion",
            "content": "Macfox wheelie riders aren’t just cyclists — they’re performers. From teens learning backyard lifts to creators filming viral rides, this movement celebrates balance, creativity, and control. Join the Macfox community and push what an electric bike can really do."
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "describe_card_mjJeaD",
        "describe_card_FX7BVr",
        "describe_card_qW3Y6Q",
        "describe_card_PA7xnE"
      ],
      "name": "Custom Collections Describe",
      "settings": {
        "title": "The Macfox Wheelie Electric Bike Collection — Balance, Control, and Pure Fun",
        "describe": "Wheelie e-bikes represent more than just power — they’re about mastering control and expression. Macfox builds electric bikes that make throttle precision, geometry balance, and visual attitude part of your ride. Whether you’re learning your first lift or filming your next combo, these bikes keep your wheel steady and your style sharp."
      }
    },
    "custom_product_tabs_zy6jqD": {
      "type": "custom-product-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "tab_item_fqezjd": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I do wheelies on a Macfox e-bike?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>Yes, you can. While Macfox bikes aren’t built specifically for wheelies, their strong rear-drive torque and balanced frames make controlled lifts possible on most models.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_yhBtqQ": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which model is easiest for wheelies?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>All models can lift with skill, but the X7’s larger rear tire gives better traction, and the X2’s dual suspension helps with smooth landings. Riders often start with these for more stability.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_EhHYNc": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is it safe to practice wheelies on an electric bike?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>Yes—if done carefully. Always wear protective gear, practice at low speeds, and use a safe open area. Gradually learn throttle response before attempting higher lifts.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_xkTHbL": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will doing wheelies damage my e-bike?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>Not if you ride responsibly. Avoid sudden throttle bursts or hard landings. Macfox frames are durable, but repeated heavy impact can wear out tires and suspension faster.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_WQHpLK": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can beginners learn to do wheelies on an e-bike?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>Yes, but start small. Focus on throttle feel and weight shift before full lifts. Many riders find e-bikes easier for balance because of their steady torque output.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_kxxUbA": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What’s the best way to improve wheelie control?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>Practice throttle finesse and rear brake timing. Many riders use short, steady lifts before extending distance. The goal is control—not just height.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_ccUNKf": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is wheelie riding legal on public roads?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>Wheelies are considered stunts, not standard riding. They should only be practiced off-road or in private areas to comply with safety and local laws.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_VebhqV": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does wheelie practice shorten battery life?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>Frequent short bursts of throttle can use more energy, but normal wheelie sessions won’t significantly reduce battery health. Proper charging habits matter more.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_MT3yfV": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do heavier riders find wheelies harder?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>Heavier riders may need more torque and careful balance, but models like the <strong>X2</strong> or <strong>X7</strong> offer enough power and stability for most users with practice.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_item_UhV3CT": {
          "type": "tab-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do I need a special throttle mode for wheelies?",
            "t_icon": "",
            "t_color": "#ffffff",
            "content": "<p>No special mode is required. The key is smooth throttle control—Macfox’s responsive motor system helps riders maintain balance and lift consistency.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
